+# Threshold Gating for `frai eval` - Implementation Summary
+
+## Feature Overview
+Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option to `frai eval` command to gate CI jobs on metric performance. Thresholds work for both CLI and SDK users.
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### 1. Core Functions (frai-core/src/eval/index.js)
+
+#### `parseThresholds(thresholdStrings = [])`
+- Parses array of threshold strings like `['exact_match=0.9', 'toxicity=0.95']`
+- Validates format: `<metric>=<number>`
+- Validates range: value must be 0 ≤ v ≤ 1
+- Returns object: `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`
+- Throws descriptive errors for malformed/invalid input
+
+#### `validateThresholds(thresholds, evaluations)`
+- Validates thresholds against available metric IDs
+- Returns `{ valid: true }` if all metrics exist
+- Returns `{ valid: false, error: "..." }` with list of valid metric IDs if unknown metric found
+- Enables helpful error messages listing all available metrics
+
+#### `checkThresholds(thresholds, evaluations)`
+- Checks if metric scores meet threshold minimums
+- Returns `{ passed: true/false, results: [...] }`
+- Each result: `{ metric, min, score, passed }`
+- Treats null scores as failures (metric with no score fails threshold)
+
+#### Modified `generateReport()`
+- Accepts optional `thresholds` parameter
+- Calls `checkThresholds()` if thresholds provided
+- Adds `passed: true/false` to report
+- Adds `thresholds: [...]` array to report
+- Maintains backward compatibility: no thresholds = no new fields
+
+### 2. CLI Integration (frai-cli/src/index.ts)
+
+#### `EvalOptions` interface
+```typescript
+interface EvalOptions {
+  outputs: string;
+  references?: string;
+  report?: string;
+  format?: 'json' | 'markdown';
+  threshold?: string[];  // New field
+}
+```
+
+#### `runEvalCommand()` updates
+1. Parse thresholds with error handling → exit code 2 for malformed
+2. Load dataset and run evaluations
+3. Validate thresholds against evaluations → exit code 2 for unknown metric
+4. Generate report with thresholds
+5. Exit code 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass
+
+#### `frai eval` command
+```
+--threshold <metric>=<min>    Repeatable option for each threshold
+```
+
+### 3. Report Format
+
+#### JSON Report
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": true,              // NEW
+  "thresholds": [              // NEW
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 0.95,
+      "passed": true
+    },
+    ...
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+#### Markdown Report
+```markdown
+## Thresholds
+
+- **exact_match:** PASS (minimum: 0.9, score: 0.95)
+- **toxicity:** FAIL (minimum: 0.99, score: 0.98)
+```
+
+## Exit Codes
+- **0** - All thresholds passed (or no thresholds specified)
+- **1** - One or more thresholds failed
+- **2** - Malformed threshold or unknown metric ID
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### CLI
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.95 \
+  --format markdown \
+  --report eval-report
+```
+
+### SDK
+```javascript
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const dataset = Eval.loadDataset({
+  outputsPath: './outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: './refs.json'
+});
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: dataset.outputs,
+  references: dataset.references
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: dataset.outputsPath,
+  referencesPath: dataset.referencesPath,
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }
+});
+
+Eval.writeReport({
+  report,
+  format: 'json',
+  reportPath: 'eval-report.json'
+});
+
+// Gate: fail if thresholds not met
+if (!report.passed) {
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+## Edge Cases Handled
+1. **Metric with null score** - Fails threshold instead of crashing
+2. **No thresholds provided** - Reports and exit codes stay exactly as before
+3. **Custom metrics** - Works transparently with metrics passed to `runEvaluations()`
+4. **Empty thresholds object** - Treated as no thresholds provided
+5. **Unknown metric** - Clear error listing valid metric IDs
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+- ✓ Without `--threshold`, `frai eval` behaves identically to before
+- ✓ SDK users can omit `thresholds` parameter
+- ✓ Reports without thresholds have no `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+- ✓ Existing Markdown/JSON parsers see new optional fields only
+
+## Testing
+Added 13 new test cases covering:
+- Threshold parsing and validation
+- Error cases (malformed, out-of-range, unknown metrics)
+- Threshold checking logic
+- Null score handling
+- Report generation with and without thresholds
+- Multiple thresholds in single report
+
+## Documentation Updates
+- ✓ README.md: CLI usage and SDK example
+- ✓ docs/eval_harness_design.md: Threshold gating section with API details
