 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Gating
+- `frai eval` accepts `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (repeatable) to gate CI on metric performance.
+- A threshold passes when the metric's score is at least the minimum (0 to 1).
+- Metrics with null scores (e.g., exact match without references) fail their threshold.
+- Exit code: 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 if threshold/metric is malformed or unknown.
+- Reports include a `passed` boolean and `thresholds` list with per-threshold results (JSON and Markdown).
+- Core API: `parseThresholds(strings)`, `validateThresholds(thresholds, evaluations)`, `checkThresholds(thresholds, evaluations)`.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object for SDK users; threshold logic is transparent to custom metrics.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
